<title>FRANCE: U.S. top source for Paris March airfreight imports.</title>
<headline>U.S. top source for Paris March airfreight imports.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. was the main country of origin for import traffic handled at the Paris airports in March 1997, airport authority(ADP) figures show.</p>
<p>Overall March 1997 import traffic to the Paris airports, , totalled 50,877 tonnes, a rise of 4.8 percent on the same month the previous year.</p>
<p>The 20 leading countries of origin for ADP imports in March 1997, with percentage change on March 1996, in parentheses, were as follows:</p>
<p>   1.  U.S		 14,073 tonnes	    +0.8 pct</p>
<p>   2.  Japan		2,466 tonnes	   +47.3</p>
<p>   3.  India		2,341 tonnes	   -12.2</p>
<p>   4.  U.K.		 2,221 tonnes	   +78.9</p>
<p>   5.  Canada	     2,031 tonnes	   -19.4</p>
<p>   6.  Hong Kong	  1,978 tonnes	   +41.2</p>
<p>   7.  Thailand	   1,452 tonnes	   +51.8</p>
<p>   8.  Fr.West Indies   1,452 tonnes	    +3.0</p>
<p>   9.  Germany	    1,422 tonnes	   +11.6</p>
<p>   10. Singapore	  1,090 tonnes	   +85.1</p>
<p>   11. Senegal		958 tonnes	    +4.2</p>
<p>   12. Italy		  936 tonnes	   -12.3</p>
<p>   13. Kenya		  891 tonnes	   -18.2</p>
<p>   14. Brazil		 764 tonnes	   +39.4</p>
<p>   15. Argentina	    712 tonnes	    +5.5</p>
<p>   16. Morocco		708 tonnes	   -28.1</p>
<p>   17. Korea		  700 tonnes	   +43.0</p>
<p>   18. Egypt		  632 tonnes	   +11.6</p>
<p>   19. China		  570 tonnes	   +40.7</p>
<p>   20. U.A.E.		 560 tonnes	   -14.7</p>
<p>-Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542-7706 Fax+5017</p>
</text>
